%% NEVER EDIT BY HAND: BBT overwrites it without asking. Once the Zotero
%% collection is wired up (SETUP.md 3.5) the example entries below disappear.
%% Commit both .bib files: they are build inputs and the journal needs them.
%%
%%   references.zotero.bib --(uv run tools/ads_enrich.py)--> references.bib
%%                                            [GENERATED] --> \bibliography{}
%%
%% Journal macros (\apj, \aj, \mnras) are NOT fixed here -- the connector writes
%% full journal names and ads_enrich.py converts them downstream (SETUP.md 3.6).
%%
%% Getting entries in: the browser connector on an ADS abstract page writes an
%% `ADS Bibcode:' line into Extra, which the BBT citation-key formula reads
%% (SETUP.md 3.3). If it is missing, the ADS translator broke and the connector
%% fell back to generic Embedded Metadata -- re-save the item. For batches use
%% ADS -> Export -> Bibcodes with Zotero's Add Item by Identifier; bulk
%% connector saves from search-result pages attach PDFs to the wrong records.
%%
%% The entries below are real ADS records, so a fresh clone compiles.

